# S9 — ai-judge-scoring (QM), census docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S9.
# See tests/models/ai-judge-scoring.oracle.ts for the oracle spec.
#
# The deterministic scoring pipeline in `reviewVariantExamWithAi`
# (apps/extensions/question-maker/app/backend/src/services/assessmentVariantService.js:1117-1226) —
# the AI judge call itself (which produces the five rubric scores +
# distinctness + usability) is out of scope; this model tests the pure
# arithmetic applied to those scores once returned. Each of the five rubric
# dimensions gets an independent Low(1)/High(5) value specifically so
# pairwise coverage can catch a swapped composite weight (0.24 vs 0.19)
# between any two dimensions. `Usability` includes "unknown" to lock in
# `normalizeUsability`'s unknown -> unusable mapping (the harshest arm)
# explicitly. `ApplyUsabilityPenalty` exists because the usability
# multiplier is applied unconditionally to the PER-QUESTION adjusted score
# but only conditionally to the exam-level final score — two different
# toggles on the same multiplier, asserted here as distinct outcomes.
ConceptualEquivalence:   low, high
DifficultySimilarity:    low, high
StructuralValidity:      low, high
AnswerCorrectness:       low, high
TopicAlignment:          low, high
Distinctness:            low, mid, high
Usability:               usable_as_is, usable_with_edits, unusable, unknown
ApplyUsabilityPenalty:   true, false
